Rename this file to portable.txt and place it next to ClipStash.exe.

ClipStash will then keep everything it stores - your settings, logs,
download history and any yt-dlp updates - in a "Data" folder beside the
program, instead of in your Windows user profile.

That makes the whole installation self-contained, so it can be copied to
a USB stick and used on another computer with your settings intact.

Delete portable.txt to go back to storing things in the normal place.
Nothing is moved automatically when you switch, so copy the Data folder
across yourself if you want to keep your history.
